{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>These are the names of the men.</b> Now, had He not already mentioned ״ואלה שמותם״? Rather, it comes to teach that these were their names for all time and were not changed, as in the case of Hoshea." "<b>And Moshe called Hoshea the son of Nun Yehoshua.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted it with reference to the addition of the yod: that Moshe prayed on his behalf — יה יושיעך, 'May YHWH save you' — from the counsel of the spies, for through the holy spirit he foresaw that they were destined to bring forth an evil report, and therefore he prayed for him. And they further gave another reason for it: Yehoshua and Kalev, who stood firm in their faith, took their reward. To Kalev, Hevron was given, as it is said (Judges 1:20): ״ויתנו לכלב את חברון״; Yehoshua took the reward of the ten spies in the land, as is written concerning the ten spies (Numbers 14:37): ״וימותו האנשים מוציאי דבת הארץ רעה״, and immediately after it: ״ויהושע בן נון וכלב בן יפונה חיו מן האנשים״ — these perished and those remained in their place. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted it: they rose in their stead for life, that is, for inheritance; and therefore the yod was added to him." "<b>And it appears</b> from here that before the sending of the spies, Hoshea was his name. If so, one may ask why the Torah mentions him by the name Yehoshua several times before this mission — as it is written (Exodus 33:11): ״ומשרתו יהושע בן נון נער״, and it is written (Exodus 33:24 [sic]): ״ויקם משה ויהושע משרתו״, and likewise (Numbers 11:28): ״ויען יהושע בן נון משרת משה״. And we may say that in honor of Moshe, who was destined to call him Yehoshua, the Torah did not wish to mention him by any other name. And the fact that it mentions him here below: למטה אפרים הושע בן נון — here it revealed to us that his original name was Hoshea, and Moshe, at this mission, called him Yehoshua. And so we find with Batyah the daughter of Pharaoh, who named him Moshe: and in her honor, since she was a king's daughter and converted, the Holy One, blessed be He, did not call him by any other name but that one."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {2 "Rabbeinu Bahya cites Exodus 33:24 for ויקם משה ויהושע משרתו, but this verse is at Exodus 24:13; the citation 33:24 appears to be a misattribution preserved as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:06.473752911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}